  "chapter": 55,
  "sortOrder": 19055,
  "verseCount": 23,
  "aliases": [
    "Psalm",
    "Psalms",
    "Ps",
    "Psa",
    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Give ear to my prayer, O God; and hide not thyself from my supplication.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Attend unto me, and hear me: I mourn in my complaint, and make a noise;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Because of the voice of the enemy, because of the oppression of the wicked: for they cast iniquity upon me, and in wrath they hate me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "My heart is sore pained within me: and the terrors of death are fallen upon me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Fearfulness and trembling are come upon me, and horror hath overwhelmed me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "And I said, Oh that I had wings like a dove! for then would I fly away, and be at rest.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Lo, then would I wander far off, and remain in the wilderness. Selah.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "I would hasten my escape from the windy storm and tempest.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Destroy, O Lord, and divide their tongues: for I have seen violence and strife in the city.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Day and night they go about it upon the walls thereof: mischief also and sorrow are in the midst of it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Wickedness is in the midst thereof: deceit and guile depart not from her streets.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "For it was not an enemy that reproached me; then I could have borne it: neither was it he that hated me that did magnify himself against me; then I would have hid myself from him:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "But it was thou, a man mine equal, my guide, and mine acquaintance.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "We took sweet counsel together, and walked unto the house of God in company.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Let death seize upon them, and let them go down quick into hell: for wickedness is in their dwellings, and among them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "As for me, I will call upon God; and the LORD shall save me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Evening, and morning, and at noon, will I pray, and cry aloud: and he shall hear my voice.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "He hath delivered my soul in peace from the battle that was against me: for there were many with me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "God shall hear, and afflict them, even he that abideth of old. Selah. Because they have no changes, therefore they fear not God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "He hath put forth his hands against such as be at peace with him: he hath broken his covenant.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "The words of his mouth were smoother than butter, but war was in his heart: his words were softer than oil, yet were they drawn swords.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Cast thy burden upon the LORD, and he shall sustain thee: he shall never suffer the righteous to be moved.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:55:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "But thou, O God, shalt bring them down into the pit of destruction: bloody and deceitful men shall not live out half their days; but I will trust in thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 55:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:55:23"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
